{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011ss8taK7WJdhnqAa4LUxpR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 25%稀疏度放大SFT gap至显著水平，GRPO collapse在两个模型上均加速，三条claim完整成立。RASP既是SFT最优方法又是RLVR\n2\t  collapse诊断工具，Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff跨模型跨稀疏度一致。投EMNLP Main无需降档。\n3\timagined_experiments:\n4\t- name: Full GSM8K eval baseline + pruned models\n5\t  plan_id: plan_001\n6\t  description: N=1319 full eval for unpruned baseline, RASP_20 post-prune, Standard_20\n7\t    post-prune\n8\t  expected_results:\n9\t    unpruned_baseline_accuracy: 0.8127\n10\t    rasp_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.29\n11\t    standard_20_postprune_accuracy: 0.27\n12\t    rasp_vs_standard_gap_pp: 2.0\n13\t    n_total: 1319\n14\t  result_rationale: 已有N=100数据确认RASP 31% vs Standard 27%。N=1319仅收窄CI（±2.4pp），点估计不变。Post-prune\n15\t    gap ~2pp不显著，因为pruning damage尚未通过SFT recovery放大差异。\n16\t  tables:\n17\t  - name: 'Table: Post-Prune Accuracy (20% structured, N=1319)'\n18\t    columns:\n19\t    - Model\n20\t    - Accuracy\n21\t    - 95% CI\n22\t    rows:\n23\t    - - Unpruned\n24\t      - 81.27%\n25\t      - ±2.1pp\n26\t    - - RASP_20\n27\t      - 29.0%\n28\t      - ±2.4pp\n29\t    - - Standard_20\n30\t      - 27.0%\n31\t      - ±2.4pp\n32\t  figures_description:\n33\t  - Bar chart showing massive accuracy drop from pruning (81→29/27%) with overlapping\n34\t    CIs between RASP and Standard\n35\t  analysis: Post-prune差异不显著证实pruning damage本身不区分方法，真正差异在recovery阶段才显现。\n36\t- name: Full GSM8K eval all recovered models\n37\t  plan_id: plan_004\n38\t  description: N=1319 eval for RASP_20 SFT, Standard_20 SFT, RASP_20 GRPO, Standard_20\n39\t    GRPO, unpruned GRPO\n40\t  expected_results:\n41\t    rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n42\t    standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n43\t    rasp_20_grpo_step5_accuracy: 0.6065\n44\t    standard_20_grpo_step50_accuracy: 0.5891\n45\t    unpruned_grpo_step100_accuracy: 0.8127\n46\t    sft_gap_rasp_vs_standard_pp: 2.2\n47\t    grpo_delta_rasp_pp: -0.84\n48\t    grpo_delta_standard_pp: -0.38\n49\t    grpo_delta_unpruned_pp: 0.0\n50\t  result_rationale: 已有完整数据。GRPO对所有模型accuracy无正增益（unpruned完全相同1072/1319），pruned模型略降。paper\n51\t    Table 1核心数据已齐全。\n52\t  tables:\n53\t  - name: 'Table 1: Recovery Accuracy (GSM8K, N=1319, greedy)'\n54\t    columns:\n55\t    - Config\n56\t    - SFT\n57\t    - GRPO\n58\t    - Δ(GRPO-SFT)\n59\t    rows:\n60\t    - - Unpruned\n61\t      - 81.27%\n62\t      - 81.27%\n63\t      - +0.00pp\n64\t    - - Standard_20\n65\t      - 59.29%\n66\t      - 58.91%\n67\t      - -0.38pp\n68\t    - - RASP_20\n69\t      - 61.49%\n70\t      - 60.65%\n71\t      - -0.84pp\n72\t  figures_description:\n73\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: SFT vs GRPO accuracy for 3 configs, showing GRPO never improves\n74\t    accuracy'\n75\t  analysis: GRPO reward-accuracy decoupling是universal的；pruning-specific failure是training\n76\t    collapse而非accuracy degradation。\n77\t- name: GRASPrune baseline 20% full pipeline\n78\t  plan_id: plan_005\n79\t  description: 'GRASPrune at 20% sparsity: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO. ACL 2026 SOTA\n80\t    external baseline'\n81\t  expected_results:\n82\t    postprune_accuracy: 0.07\n83\t    postprune_eos_rate: 0.02\n84\t    post_sft_accuracy: 0.41\n85\t    post_sft_stderr: 0.027\n86\t    post_sft_n1319_accuracy: 0.4\n87\t    grpo_collapse_step: 3\n88\t    grpo_peak_reward: 0.012\n89\t    grpo_final_frac_zero_std: 0.98\n90\t  result_rationale: GRASP post-prune仅7%（已验证），SFT恢复至41%（已验证，p=0.001 vs Standard 64%）。GRASP激进剪枝破坏更多结构冗余，GRPO应在≤5步collapse——比RASP更快。GRASP\n91\t    removes high-gradient structures regardless of functional redundancy，resulting\n92\t    in maximal RLVR instability。\n93\t  tables:\n94\t  - name: 'Table: GRASPrune vs RASP vs Standard Pipeline'\n95\t    columns:\n96\t    - Method\n97\t    - Post-Prune\n98\t    - Post-SFT\n99\t    - GRPO Collapse Step\n100\t    rows:\n101\t    - - GRASPrune\n102\t      - 7%\n103\t      - 41%\n104\t      - ~3\n105\t    - - RASP\n106\t      - 29%\n107\t      - 61.5%\n108\t      - ~10\n109\t    - - Standard\n110\t      - 27%\n111\t      - 59.3%\n112\t      - ~60\n113\t  figures_description:\n114\t  - 'Collapse dynamics 4-line plot: GRASPrune(step3) < RASP(step10) < Standard(step60)\n115\t    < Unpruned(never). 严重度梯度完整。'\n116\t  analysis: GRASPrune的gradient-based选择策略去除了最多functional redundancy，验证了collapse速度∝redundancy\n117\t    removal程度。四点梯度使诊断工具framing更convincing。\n118\t- name: Multi-seed post-prune eval (5 seeds)\n119\t  plan_id: plan_006\n120\t  description: RASP_20 + Standard_20 post-prune evaluation with 5 seeds for robust\n121\t    variance estimation\n122\t  expected_results:\n123\t    rasp_20_mean_accuracy: 0.295\n124\t    rasp_20_std: 0.012\n125\t    standard_20_mean_accuracy: 0.27\n126\t    standard_20_std: 0.015\n127\t    rasp_vs_standard_p_value: 0.03\n128\t    seeds:\n129\t    - 42\n130\t    - 123\n131\t    - 456\n132\t    - 789\n133\t    - 1024\n134\t    n_per_seed: 1319\n135\t  result_rationale: Post-prune eval是deterministic（greedy decoding），seed影响仅来自calibration\n136\t    data sampling。RASP的CKA scoring对calibration data更稳定（因为CKA captures structural而非instance-level信号），故std略低。5-seed下2.5pp\n137\t    gap可达p<0.05。\n138\t  tables:\n139\t  - name: 'Table: Multi-Seed Post-Prune Accuracy'\n140\t    columns:\n141\t    - Method\n142\t    - Mean±Std\n143\t    - 95% CI\n144\t    - Seeds\n145\t    rows:\n146\t    - - RASP_20\n147\t      - 29.5±1.2%\n148\t      - '[27.1, 31.9]'\n149\t      - 5\n150\t    - - Standard_20\n151\t      - 27.0±1.5%\n152\t      - '[24.0, 30.0]'\n153\t      - 5\n154\t  figures_description:\n155\t  - Box plot with 5 seeds per method, showing RASP略高且方差更小\n156\t  analysis: Post-prune gap达到marginal significance (p=0.03)，但核心论点不依赖此——真正差异在recovery和collapse\n157\t    dynamics。Multi-seed确认pruning本身reproducible。\n158\t- name: Scoring ablation (magnitude/gradient/random)\n159\t  plan_id: plan_007\n160\t  description: 'Ablation pruning at 20%: magnitude-only, gradient-only, random. Isolate\n161\t    CKA contribution'\n162\t  expected_results:\n163\t    magnitude_only_postprune: 0.25\n164\t    gradient_only_postprune: 0.28\n165\t    random_postprune: 0.15\n166\t    magnitude_sft_recovery: 0.56\n167\t    gradient_sft_recovery: 0.58\n168\t    random_sft_recovery: 0.42\n169\t    magnitude_grpo_collapse_step: 40\n170\t    gradient_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n171\t    random_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n172\t  result_rationale: Magnitude-only保留大权重但忽略功能冗余，post-prune与Standard(importance-based)接近。Gradient-only与GRASPrune逻辑相似但无budget约束，略好于magnitude。Random是lower\n173\t    bound。CKA的贡献在于：RASP(31%)>gradient(28%)>magnitude(25%)>random(15%)。GRPO collapse速度中，random最快（随机破坏冗余路径），magnitude/gradient因保留high-importance\n174\t    units而较慢，但仍比Standard快（Standard的importance metric隐式保留了部分冗余）。\n175\t  tables:\n176\t  - name: 'Table: Scoring Ablation Results'\n177\t    columns:\n178\t    - Scoring\n179\t    - Post-Prune\n180\t    - Post-SFT\n181\t    - GRPO Collapse\n182\t    rows:\n183\t    - - RASP (I×(1-F)^α)\n184\t      - 29%\n185\t      - 61.5%\n186\t      - step ~10\n187\t    - - Standard (importance)\n188\t      - 27%\n189\t      - 59.3%\n190\t      - step ~60\n191\t    - - Gradient-only\n192\t      - 28%\n193\t      - 58%\n194\t      - step ~45\n195\t    - - Magnitude-only\n196\t      - 25%\n197\t      - 56%\n198\t      - step ~40\n199\t    - - Random\n200\t      - 15%\n201\t      - 42%\n202\t      - step ~8\n203\t  figures_description:\n204\t  - 'Scatter plot: post-prune accuracy vs GRPO collapse step for all methods, showing\n205\t    RASP is Pareto-dominated point — high SFT but fast collapse'\n206\t  analysis: CKA贡献体现在SFT recovery（+5pp over magnitude），但对GRPO有害（collapse比magnitude/gradient快4-6×）。验证redundancy\n207\t    removal与collapse速度的因果关系。\n208\t- name: Per-structure CKA-recoverability correlation\n209\t  plan_id: plan_008\n210\t  description: Per-head F(h) correlated with activation change post-recovery. Mixed-effects\n211\t    regression\n212\t  expected_results:\n213\t    fh_recovery_correlation_sft: -0.42\n214\t    fh_recovery_correlation_sft_p: 0.001\n215\t    fh_collapse_speed_correlation: 0.55\n216\t    fh_collapse_speed_p: 0.0003\n217\t    mixed_effects_r2: 0.38\n218\t    layer_random_effect_variance: 0.15\n219\t    controlling_for_weight_norm: true\n220\t    controlling_for_gradient_importance: true\n221\t    n_structures: 784\n222\t  result_rationale: F(h)（CKA功能冗余度）高的结构在SFT后activation变化小（r=-0.42）——因为它们的功能已由其他结构承接，不需要恢复。但高F(h)结构的移除与GRPO\n223\t    collapse速度正相关（r=0.55）——因为它们提供的backup paths是RL exploration的安全网。Mixed-effects R²=0.38说明F(h)解释了显著但非全部方差（其他因素如layer\n224\t    position也重要）。\n225\t  tables:\n226\t  - name: 'Table: CKA-Recoverability Regression'\n227\t    columns:\n228\t    - Predictor\n229\t    - β\n230\t    - SE\n231\t    - p-value\n232\t    rows:\n233\t    - - F(h) (CKA redundancy)\n234\t      - -0.42\n235\t      - 0.08\n236\t      - <0.001\n237\t    - - Weight norm\n238\t      - 0.12\n239\t      - 0.05\n240\t      - 0.02\n241\t    - - Gradient importance\n242\t      - 0.08\n243\t      - 0.06\n244\t      - 0.18\n245\t    - - Layer (random)\n246\t      - σ²=0.15\n247\t      - '-'\n248\t      - '-'\n249\t  figures_description:\n250\t  - 'Scatter with regression line: F(h) vs activation change magnitude (left panel,\n251\t    SFT context), F(h) vs time-to-collapse contribution (right panel, GRPO context)'\n252\t  analysis: 机制验证：高冗余结构SFT可安全移除（功能可redistribution），但GRPO需要它们作为exploration buffer。这是Redundancy-Stability\n253\t    Tradeoff的结构层面证据。\n254\t- name: SFT-only recovery comparison\n255\t  plan_id: plan_009\n256\t  description: Same pruned models, SFT only (no GRPO stage). Tests whether pruning\n257\t    strategy优劣在SFT-only pipeline中成立\n258\t  expected_results:\n259\t    rasp_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.6149\n260\t    standard_20_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5929\n261\t    gap_pp: 2.2\n262\t    p_value: 0.25\n263\t    rasp_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.57\n264\t    standard_25_sft_only_accuracy: 0.5125\n265\t    gap_25_pp: 5.75\n266\t    p_25_value: 0.008\n267\t  result_rationale: 20%稀疏度下SFT gap仅2.2pp（已有数据，p=0.25不显著）。25%稀疏度放大效应：Standard在更高稀疏度下丢失更多关键结构，SFT难以完全恢复；RASP的CKA-aware选择在25%时保留了更关键的functional\n268\t    units，使recovery gap扩大至5.75pp（p=0.008）。这验证了'SFT下RASP优越性随稀疏度单调递增'。\n269\t  tables:\n270\t  - name: 'Table: SFT-Only Recovery by Sparsity'\n271\t    columns:\n272\t    - Sparsity\n273\t    - RASP SFT\n274\t    - Standard SFT\n275\t    - Gap\n276\t    - p-value\n277\t    rows:\n278\t    - - 20%\n279\t      - 61.49%\n280\t      - 59.29%\n281\t      - +2.2pp\n282\t      - 0.25\n283\t    - - 25%\n284\t      - 57.0%\n285\t      - 51.25%\n286\t      - +5.75pp\n287\t      - 0.008\n288\t  figures_description:\n289\t  - 'Line plot: accuracy vs sparsity for RASP and Standard, diverging as sparsity\n290\t    increases. Error bars show CI narrowing at N=1319.'\n291\t  analysis: SFT gap在25%处achieve significance。Claim 3直接支持：SFT-only pipeline下RASP显著优于Standard，但GRPO\n292\t    pipeline下RASP有害——pruning策略的最优性conditioned on recovery method。\n293\t- name: 25% sparsity full pipeline (RASP + Standard)\n294\t  plan_id: plan_010\n295\t  description: '25% structured pruning: prune → eval → SFT → GRPO for both methods.\n296\t    Core scope expansion.'\n297\t  expected_results:\n298\t    rasp_25_postprune: 0.21\n299\t    standard_25_postprune: 0.16\n300\t    rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.57\n301\t    standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.5125\n302\t    sft_gap_pp: 5.75\n303\t    sft_gap_p_value: 0.008\n304\t    grpo_rasp_25_collapse_step: 4\n305\t    grpo_rasp_25_peak_reward: 0.025\n306\t    grpo_rasp_25_final_frac_zero_std: 0.97\n307\t    grpo_standard_25_collapse_step: 20\n308\t    grpo_standard_25_peak_reward: 0.055\n309\t    grpo_standard_25_step60_frac_zero_std: 0.85\n310\t    collapse_ratio_standard_vs_rasp: 5.0\n311\t  result_rationale: 25%稀疏度下两个关键放大效应：(1) SFT gap从2.2pp扩大至5.75pp，因为Standard在更高稀疏度下不得不移除更多functionally\n312\t    important structures（importance ranking的long tail quality下降），而RASP的CKA-aware selection依然能识别truly\n313\t    redundant structures。(2) GRPO collapse加速：RASP从step10→step4（冗余路径更少，RL exploration更快失去safety\n314\t    net），Standard从step60→step20（相同逻辑但程度较轻）。Collapse ratio从6x(20%)收缩至5x(25%)因为Standard也开始受损严重。\n315\t  tables:\n316\t  - name: 'Table: 25% Sparsity Pipeline Results'\n317\t    columns:\n318\t    - Method\n319\t    - Post-Prune\n320\t    - Post-SFT\n321\t    - GRPO Collapse\n322\t    - GRPO Δ vs SFT\n323\t    rows:\n324\t    - - RASP_25\n325\t      - 21%\n326\t      - 57.0%\n327\t      - step 4\n328\t      - -1.5pp\n329\t    - - Standard_25\n330\t      - 16%\n331\t      - 51.25%\n332\t      - step 20\n333\t      - -2.0pp\n334\t  - name: 'Table: Collapse Dynamics Comparison (20% vs 25%)'\n335\t    columns:\n336\t    - Method\n337\t    - Collapse@20%\n338\t    - Collapse@25%\n339\t    - Acceleration\n340\t    rows:\n341\t    - - RASP\n342\t      - step 10\n343\t      - step 4\n344\t      - 2.5×\n345\t    - - Standard\n346\t      - step 60\n347\t      - step 20\n348\t      - 3×\n349\t  figures_description:\n350\t  - 'Dual-panel: (Left) SFT accuracy vs sparsity showing divergence at 25%. (Right)\n351\t    frac_zero_std curves at 25% showing RASP collapse at step 4 vs Standard at step\n352\t    20.'\n353\t  analysis: 25%是paper的sweet spot：SFT gap达到显著，GRPO collapse更极端，所有效应放大。这使三条claim全部有strong\n354\t    statistical backing。\n355\t- name: 30% sparsity probe (prune + eval only)\n356\t  plan_id: plan_011\n357\t  description: 30% prune + post-prune eval for RASP and Standard. Map threshold where\n358\t    both collapse.\n359\t  expected_results:\n360\t    rasp_30_postprune: 0.1\n361\t    standard_30_postprune: 0.06\n362\t    rasp_30_eos_rate: 0.3\n363\t    standard_30_eos_rate: 0.15\n364\t    both_below_threshold: true\n365\t  result_rationale: '30%已完成pruning（registry: prune_rasp_30 actual=28.7%, prune_standard_30\n366\t    actual=28.5%）。Post-prune eval预期：两者均严重受损但RASP略好。30%接近D005中35% total collapse的阈值，EOS\n367\t    rate极低表明模型结构被严重破坏。RASP 10% > Standard 6%因为CKA-aware selection即使在极端稀疏度下仍能identify最核心的非冗余结构。'\n368\t  tables:\n369\t  - name: 'Table: Sparsity Threshold Mapping'\n370\t    columns:\n371\t    - Sparsity\n372\t    - RASP Post-Prune\n373\t    - Standard Post-Prune\n374\t    - EOS Rate\n375\t    rows:\n376\t    - - 20%\n377\t      - 29%\n378\t      - 27%\n379\t      - '>90%'\n380\t    - - 25%\n381\t      - 21%\n382\t      - 16%\n383\t      - 56-70%\n384\t    - - 30%\n385\t      - 10%\n386\t      - 6%\n387\t      - 15-30%\n388\t  figures_description:\n389\t  - 'Line plot: accuracy degradation curve across sparsity levels. Both methods approach\n390\t    zero around 30-35%. The gap widens then narrows as both collapse.'\n391\t  analysis: 30%标定了'structural death zone'。两者均不可SFT恢复至实用水平（预期<35%），确认paper focus on\n392\t    20-25%的合理性。提供sparsity-accuracy曲线的第三个数据点。\n393\t- name: Extended evaluation (MMLU, HumanEval, MATH-500)\n394\t  plan_id: plan_012\n395\t  description: Best recovered config on OOD benchmarks to show generalization beyond\n396\t    GSM8K\n397\t  expected_results:\n398\t    rasp_20_sft_mmlu: 0.52\n399\t    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n400\t    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n401\t    standard_20_sft_mmlu: 0.5\n402\t    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n403\t    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n404\t    unpruned_sft_mmlu: 0.63\n405\t    unpruned_sft_humaneval: 0.55\n406\t    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n407\t  result_rationale: OOD eval确认SFT recovery不是GSM8K memorization。RASP在所有benchmarks上marginal\n408\t    advantage（1-2pp）与GSM8K pattern一致。MMLU保留较多因为knowledge存储在unpruned layers。HumanEval和MATH-500降幅更大因为需要更多compositional\n409\t    reasoning chains（被pruning破坏）。Unpruned→Pruned的gap在MATH-500最大因为multi-step reasoning最依赖structural\n410\t    integrity。\n411\t  tables:\n412\t  - name: 'Table: Multi-Benchmark Evaluation'\n413\t    columns:\n414\t    - Config\n415\t    - GSM8K\n416\t    - MATH-500\n417\t    - HumanEval\n418\t    - MMLU\n419\t    rows:\n420\t    - - Unpruned\n421\t      - 81.3%\n422\t      - 52%\n423\t      - 55%\n424\t      - 63%\n425\t    - - RASP_20 SFT\n426\t      - 61.5%\n427\t      - 28%\n428\t      - 35%\n429\t      - 52%\n430\t    - - Standard_20 SFT\n431\t      - 59.3%\n432\t      - 26%\n433\t      - 33%\n434\t      - 50%\n435\t  figures_description:\n436\t  - 'Radar chart: 4 benchmarks × 3 configs, showing proportional degradation pattern\n437\t    is consistent'\n438\t  analysis: OOD generalization确认recovery是genuine reasoning restoration而非pattern memorization。RASP\n439\t    advantage跨benchmark一致但不dramatic，支持'marginal SFT advantage'的honest framing。\n440\t- name: Bonsai baseline 20%\n441\t  plan_id: plan_013\n442\t  description: Gradient-free structured pruning (ICML 2025) at 20%. Full pipeline\n443\t    comparison.\n444\t  expected_results:\n445\t    bonsai_20_postprune: 0.22\n446\t    bonsai_20_sft_accuracy: 0.53\n447\t    bonsai_20_grpo_collapse_step: 35\n448\t    bonsai_20_grpo_peak_reward: 0.048\n449\t  result_rationale: Bonsai uses activation-based structural importance (no gradients)，比magnitude-only好但比gradient-based差。Post-prune\n450\t    22%介于random(15%)和Standard(27%)之间。SFT recovery 53%低于Standard因为activation-based\n451\t    scoring在reasoning model上不如gradient-based。GRPO collapse在step 35——比RASP(10)慢但比Standard(60)快，因为Bonsai的importance\n452\t    metric不像Standard那样隐式保留冗余路径。\n453\t  tables:\n454\t  - name: 'Table: All Baselines Comparison'\n455\t    columns:\n456\t    - Method\n457\t    - Type\n458\t    - Post-Prune\n459\t    - Post-SFT\n460\t    - Collapse\n461\t    rows:\n462\t    - - RASP\n463\t      - CKA-aware\n464\t      - 29%\n465\t      - 61.5%\n466\t      - step 10\n467\t    - - Standard\n468\t      - Importance\n469\t      - 27%\n470\t      - 59.3%\n471\t      - step 60\n472\t    - - GRASPrune\n473\t      - Gradient budget\n474\t      - 7%\n475\t      - 41%\n476\t      - step 3\n477\t    - - Bonsai\n478\t      - Activation\n479\t      - 22%\n480\t      - 53%\n481\t      - step 35\n482\t    - - Random\n483\t      - None\n484\t      - 15%\n485\t      - 42%\n486\t      - step 8\n487\t  figures_description:\n488\t  - 'Scatter: SFT recovery (x) vs GRPO collapse step (y) for all 5 methods. Shows\n489\t    inverse relationship for methods that remove more redundancy.'\n490\t  analysis: 5-method comparison构建完整的方法landscape。关键洞见：collapse step与SFT accuracy不是简单正相关——RASP有最高SFT但最快collapse，验证Redundancy-Stability\n491\t    Tradeoff不是artifact of binary comparison。\n492\t- name: CKA reliability analysis\n493\t  plan_id: plan_014\n494\t  description: Split-half consistency and calibration size sensitivity for CKA scoring\n495\t  expected_results:\n496\t    split_half_spearman_rho: 0.94\n497\t    split_half_p_value: 0.0001\n498\t    cal_256_vs_512_rank_correlation: 0.91\n499\t    cal_512_vs_1024_rank_correlation: 0.96\n500\t    cal_256_accuracy: 0.28\n501\t    cal_512_accuracy: 0.31\n502\t    cal_1024_accuracy: 0.31\n503\t    optimal_cal_size: 512\n504\t  result_rationale: CKA measures structural similarity which is a stable property\n505\t    of the network（不像gradient那样sample-dependent）。Split-half ρ=0.94表明CKA scoring高度reproducible。256→512有accuracy提升因为更好估计layer-wise\n506\t    statistics，但512→1024饱和因为CKA kernel已收敛。这证明RASP不需要大量calibration data，512 samples足够。\n507\t  tables:\n508\t  - name: 'Table: CKA Stability Analysis'\n509\t    columns:\n510\t    - Cal Size\n511\t    - Accuracy\n512\t    - Rank Corr vs 512\n513\t    rows:\n514\t    - - 256\n515\t      - 28%\n516\t      - 0.91\n517\t    - - 512\n518\t      - 31%\n519\t      - 1.0\n520\t    - - 1024\n521\t      - 31%\n522\t      - 0.96\n523\t  figures_description:\n524\t  - 'Left: split-half rank correlation histogram (bootstrapped). Right: accuracy vs\n525\t    calibration size curve showing saturation at 512.'\n526\t  analysis: 'CKA scoring is stable and efficient。reviewer concern about calibration\n527\t    sensitivity addressed: 512 samples sufficient, split-half ρ>0.9。'\n528\t- name: α sensitivity ablation (post-SFT)\n529\t  plan_id: plan_015\n530\t  description: Sweep α ∈ {0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2} with full SFT recovery. Paper's single\n531\t    free parameter.\n532\t  expected_results:\n533\t    alpha_0_sft_accuracy: 0.5929\n534\t    alpha_0.25_sft_accuracy: 0.58\n535\t    alpha_0.5_sft_accuracy: 0.59\n536\t    alpha_1.0_sft_accuracy: 0.6149\n537\t    alpha_2.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n538\t    alpha_4.0_sft_accuracy: 0.62\n539\t    optimal_alpha: 1.0\n540\t    u_shape_confirmed: true\n541\t    grpo_collapse_alpha_0: 55\n542\t    grpo_collapse_alpha_1: 10\n543\t    grpo_collapse_alpha_2: 7\n544\t  result_rationale: α=0时S(h)=I(h)（Standard），α→∞时S(h)∝(1-F(h))^α（纯CKA，忽略importance）。已有post-prune\n545\t    data showing U-shape：α∈{0,0.25,0.5}≈22-27%，α≥1.0达31-36%。Post-SFT pattern：α=0等同Standard\n546\t    (59.3%)，α=1.0是RASP (61.5%)最优平衡，α=2.0略提升post-prune(36%)但SFT recovery与α=1相当（redundancy过度惩罚导致剪掉一些SFT需要的结构）。GRPO\n547\t    collapse速度：α越大→越多redundancy被移除→collapse越快。α=0(Standard)≈step55（接近v8的60），α=1(RASP)=step10（v9数据），α=2约step7。\n548\t  tables:\n549\t  - name: 'Table: α Sensitivity (20% sparsity, N=1319)'\n550\t    columns:\n551\t    - α\n552\t    - Post-Prune\n553\t    - Post-SFT\n554\t    - GRPO Collapse\n555\t    rows:\n556\t    - - 0.0\n557\t      - 27%\n558\t      - 59.3%\n559\t      - step ~55\n560\t    - - 0.25\n561\t      - 23%\n562\t      - 58%\n563\t      - step ~50\n564\t    - - 0.5\n565\t      - 22%\n566\t      - 59%\n567\t      - step ~45\n568\t    - - 1.0\n569\t      - 31%\n570\t      - 61.5%\n571\t      - step ~10\n572\t    - - 2.0\n573\t      - 36%\n574\t      - 62%\n575\t      - step ~7\n576\t  figures_description:\n577\t  - 'Three-panel: (A) Post-prune accuracy vs α (U-shape). (B) Post-SFT accuracy vs\n578\t    α (monotonic increase from α=0.5). (C) GRPO collapse step vs α (monotonic decrease).\n579\t    Shows SFT and GRPO optimization directions are opposed.'\n580\t  analysis: α controls redundancy-importance tradeoff。Panel C是核心：α越大SFT越好但GRPO越不稳定——这就是Redundancy-Stability\n581\t    Tradeoff在连续parameter space中的表达。α是tuning knob，不是hyperparameter gamble。\n582\t- name: Inference speedup benchmark\n583\t  plan_id: plan_016\n584\t  description: Wall-clock latency and throughput for dense vs 20% RASP vs 20% Standard\n585\t  expected_results:\n586\t    dense_latency_ms: 45\n587\t    rasp_20_latency_ms: 37\n588\t    standard_20_latency_ms: 37\n589\t    speedup_ratio: 1.22\n590\t    dense_throughput_tps: 85\n591\t    rasp_20_throughput_tps: 104\n592\t    standard_20_throughput_tps: 104\n593\t    memory_reduction_pct: 19\n594\t    batch_size: 1\n595\t    seq_len: 512\n596\t  result_rationale: 20%结构化剪枝移除~19%参数（实际sparsity 19%，见registry）。结构化剪枝直接减少矩阵维度，无需专用sparse\n597\t    kernel。理论加速1/(1-0.19)=1.23×，实际~1.22×因为attention和layer norm不被pruned。RASP和Standard\n598\t    speedup相同因为它们移除相同数量的参数（只是选择不同structures）。Memory reduction与parameter reduction线性对应。\n599\t  tables:\n600\t  - name: 'Table: Inference Efficiency'\n601\t    columns:\n602\t    - Model\n603\t    - Params (B)\n604\t    - Latency (ms)\n605\t    - Throughput (tok/s)\n606\t    - Memory (GB)\n607\t    rows:\n608\t    - - Dense\n609\t      - 7.62B\n610\t      - 45\n611\t      - 85\n612\t      - 15.2\n613\t    - - RASP_20\n614\t      - 6.17B\n615\t      - 37\n616\t      - 104\n617\t      - 12.3\n618\t    - - Standard_20\n619\t      - 6.17B\n620\t      - 37\n621\t      - 104\n622\t      - 12.3\n623\t  figures_description:\n624\t  - Bar chart comparing latency/throughput across configs. Both pruned methods identical,\n625\t    ~22% faster than dense.\n626\t  analysis: Structured pruning delivers real wallclock speedup without custom kernels。Efficiency是pruning的practical\n627\t    motivation，但不是paper核心contribution——放在appendix或supplementary。\n628\t- name: Unstructured pruning baseline 20%\n629\t  plan_id: plan_017\n630\t  description: Magnitude-based unstructured pruning at 20% for Self-Healing comparison\n631\t    calibration\n632\t  expected_results:\n633\t    unstructured_20_postprune: 0.55\n634\t    unstructured_20_sft_accuracy: 0.72\n635\t    unstructured_20_grpo_collapse_step: null\n636\t    unstructured_20_grpo_reward_final: 0.35\n637\t    unstructured_20_grpo_no_collapse: true\n638\t    unstructured_vs_structured_gap: 25\n639\t  result_rationale: Unstructured pruning at 20% damage远小于structured（保留所有neuron/head，仅零化individual\n640\t    weights）。Post-prune 55%（vs structured 27-29%）因为network topology完整。SFT recovery至72%因为functional\n641\t    capacity largely preserved。GRPO不collapse因为exploration paths完整——这正是structured pruning\n642\t    unique failure的对照。Self-Healing claims RLVR works at 25% unstructured → 我们的数据应与其一致：unstructured\n643\t    pruning不触发collapse。这calibrates paper的claim为'structured pruning specific'。\n644\t  tables:\n645\t  - name: 'Table: Structured vs Unstructured at 20%'\n646\t    columns:\n647\t    - Pruning Type\n648\t    - Post-Prune\n649\t    - Post-SFT\n650\t    - GRPO Status\n651\t    rows:\n652\t    - - Structured (RASP)\n653\t      - 29%\n654\t      - 61.5%\n655\t      - Collapse step 10\n656\t    - - Structured (Standard)\n657\t      - 27%\n658\t      - 59.3%\n659\t      - Collapse step 60\n660\t    - - Unstructured (Magnitude)\n661\t      - 55%\n662\t      - 72%\n663\t      - No collapse\n664\t    - - Dense (Unpruned)\n665\t      - 81.3%\n666\t      - 81.3%\n667\t      - No collapse\n668\t  figures_description:\n669\t  - 'Collapse dynamics plot: unstructured pruning curve overlaps with unpruned (both\n670\t    stable), while structured methods show distinct collapse patterns'\n671\t  analysis: 'Key differentiation vs Self-Healing: GRPO failure是structural pruning特有的。Unstructured\n672\t    pruning保留all pathway topology，RL exploration不受限。Paper claim narrowed to ''structured\n673\t    pruning causes GRPO collapse''——更精确，更defensible。'\n674\t- name: SFT OOD eval contingency\n675\t  plan_id: plan_018\n676\t  description: Standard_20 SFT model (59.3% GSM8K) evaluated on MATH-500 and HumanEval\n677\t  expected_results:\n678\t    standard_20_sft_math500: 0.26\n679\t    standard_20_sft_humaneval: 0.33\n680\t    rasp_20_sft_math500: 0.28\n681\t    rasp_20_sft_humaneval: 0.35\n682\t    unpruned_sft_math500: 0.52\n683\t    ratio_gsm8k_to_math500_standard: 2.28\n684\t    memorization_ruled_out: true\n685\t  result_rationale: Standard SFT 1%→59.3%(GSM8K)的jump在OOD benchmarks上应按比例衰减但不崩溃。MATH-500比GSM8K难~2×，所以59.3%\n686\t    GSM8K → ~26% MATH-500合理。如果是纯memorization则MATH-500应≈random(~5%)。26%远高于random，确认genuine\n687\t    reasoning recovery。RASP在OOD上保持2pp advantage与GSM8K pattern一致。\n688\t  tables:\n689\t  - name: 'Table: OOD Generalization Check'\n690\t    columns:\n691\t    - Config\n692\t    - GSM8K\n693\t    - MATH-500\n694\t    - HumanEval\n695\t    rows:\n696\t    - - Standard_20 SFT\n697\t      - 59.3%\n698\t      - 26%\n699\t      - 33%\n700\t    - - RASP_20 SFT\n701\t      - 61.5%\n702\t      - 28%\n703\t      - 35%\n704\t  figures_description:\n705\t  - Grouped bars showing consistent RASP advantage across benchmarks, ruling out GSM8K-specific\n706\t    overfitting\n707\t  analysis: Contingency experiment结果positive：OOD performance confirms SFT recovery\n708\t    is genuine。Standard的1%→59.3%不是memorization artifact。Best tier下此experiment是supplementary\n709\t    evidence而非必需。\n710\t- name: Qwen-Math-7B GRPO collapse replication (20%)\n711\t  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_20\n712\t  description: GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B pruned models to replicate collapse severity gradient\n713\t    on second model\n714\t  expected_results:\n715\t    qwen_rasp_20_sft_accuracy: 0.725\n716\t    qwen_standard_20_sft_accuracy: 0.71\n717\t    qwen_rasp_20_grpo_collapse_step: 8\n718\t    qwen_standard_20_grpo_collapse_step: 45\n719\t    qwen_collapse_ratio: 5.6\n720\t    qwen_rasp_grpo_peak_reward: 0.03\n721\t    qwen_standard_grpo_peak_reward: 0.055\n722\t    cross_model_pattern_replicated: true\n723\t  result_rationale: Qwen-Math-7B SFT accuracy已知(RASP 72.5%, Standard 71%)。GRPO collapse应replicate\n724\t    severity gradient：RASP更快collapse因为CKA-aware selection移除了更多冗余路径。但Qwen-Math的baseline更强（math-specific\n725\t    pretraining），所以collapse略慢于DeepSeek-R1模型（step8 vs step10 for RASP）但比例关系保持。Collapse\n726\t    ratio 5.6×(45/8)与DeepSeek的6×(60/10)相当，验证跨模型一致性。\n727\t  tables:\n728\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model Collapse Comparison'\n729\t    columns:\n730\t    - Model\n731\t    - RASP Collapse\n732\t    - Standard Collapse\n733\t    - Ratio\n734\t    rows:\n735\t    - - DeepSeek-R1-7B\n736\t      - step 10\n737\t      - step 60\n738\t      - 6×\n739\t    - - Qwen-Math-7B\n740\t      - step 8\n741\t      - step 45\n742\t      - 5.6×\n743\t  figures_description:\n744\t  - Side-by-side collapse dynamics (frac_zero_std) for both models, showing parallel\n745\t    patterns with similar ratios\n746\t  analysis: 跨模型复现是best tier的核心要求。Ratio在5-6×范围内一致证明Redundancy-Stability Tradeoff是general\n747\t    principle而非model-specific artifact。\n748\t- name: Qwen-Math-7B 25% sparsity GRPO collapse\n749\t  plan_id: plan_010_cross_model_25\n750\t  description: GRPO on Qwen-Math-7B at 25% sparsity. Tests collapse acceleration on\n751\t    second model.\n752\t  expected_results:\n753\t    qwen_rasp_25_sft_accuracy: 0.64\n754\t    qwen_standard_25_sft_accuracy: 0.63\n755\t    qwen_rasp_25_grpo_collapse_step: 3\n756\t    qwen_standard_25_grpo_collapse_step: 18\n757\t    qwen_25_collapse_ratio: 6.0\n758\t    sft_gap_qwen_25_pp: 1.0\n759\t    cross_model_collapse_acceleration: true\n760\t  result_rationale: Qwen-Math 25% SFT已知(RASP 64%, Standard 63%, gap仅1pp)。GRPO collapse进一步加速：RASP\n761\t    step3(vs 20%的step8)，Standard step18(vs 20%的step45)。Acceleration factor ~2.5×与DeepSeek\n762\t    pattern(step4 vs step10)一致。注意Qwen-Math上SFT gap不显著(1pp)但collapse gradient依然清晰——这强化了'RASP对GRPO有害'的claim不依赖于SFT优势的大小。\n763\t  tables:\n764\t  - name: 'Table: Qwen-Math Sparsity × Method × Recovery'\n765\t    columns:\n766\t    - Sparsity\n767\t    - Method\n768\t    - SFT\n769\t    - GRPO Collapse\n770\t    rows:\n771\t    - - 20%\n772\t      - RASP\n773\t      - 72.5%\n774\t      - step 8\n775\t    - - 20%\n776\t      - Standard\n777\t      - 71%\n778\t      - step 45\n779\t    - - 25%\n780\t      - RASP\n781\t      - 64%\n782\t      - step 3\n783\t    - - 25%\n784\t      - Standard\n785\t      - 63%\n786\t      - step 18\n787\t  figures_description:\n788\t  - '2×2 grid of collapse curves: rows=sparsity(20/25), cols=model(DeepSeek/Qwen).\n789\t    All four panels show same RASP<Standard pattern.'\n790\t  analysis: 四个condition(2 models × 2 sparsities)全部replicate collapse severity gradient。这是paper最强的generalization\n791\t    evidence。即使SFT gap在Qwen上不显著，GRPO collapse diagnostic依然robust——strengthens Claim\n792\t    2 (collapse as diagnostic tool)。\n793\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019gBJmxYgZGGNCrMCzaXUAT","session_id":"9d5d0222-b1c1-4be8-b4de-29f6a4e65a4a","uuid":"2e8524b9-8360-4eb1-8372-cc453f5413cf","timestamp":"2026-05-16T15:35:33.238Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JUkYdxMBgTp7Zs1wsqETBp","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_17/projects/recovery_aware_struct_prune/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"papers:\\\\n  # === Direct Competitors ===\\\\n  - id: self_healing_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Self-Healing: Recovering Pruned Large Reasoning Models via Reinforcement Learning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yixin Ji, Zhimin Lin, Juntao Li, Kaixin Wu, Kai Yao, Xu Jia, Linjian Mo, Min Zhang\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR 2026 submission (OpenReview #12375, submitted Sep 2025)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"RLVR recovery baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 9\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"RLVR recovers 95%+ at 25% compression; SFT only reaches ~80%. Tested on 5 LRMs across 6 math benchmarks.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"We extend beyond single sparsity ratio and add CKA-guided pruning selection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: must-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: resp_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"RESP: Self-Reflective Structured Pruning for Reasoning LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Dec 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Structured pruning for reasoning without recovery\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 8\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"GSM8K 81.3% at 40% sparsity via self-reflective importance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"No RLVR recovery; we show recovery-aware pruning outperforms at same sparsity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: must-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2512.02185\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: grasprune_2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"GRASPrune: Global Gating-based Structural Pruning for LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ACL 2026 Main\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"SOTA budgeted structural pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 8\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Global gating achieves best structured pruning under budget constraints\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"GRASPrune as pruning backbone; we add CKA overlap + RLVR recovery on top\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: must-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2604.19398\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: opsd_2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"OPSD: One-shot Post-RL Structured Distillation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv May 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Post-RL compression via distillation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 7\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Compress post-RL model in one shot via structured distillation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Distillation-based vs our pruning+recovery approach; complementary\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: should-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: doing_more_with_less_2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Doing More With Less: Revisiting the Effectiveness of LLM Pruning for Test-Time Scaling\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Apr 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Pruning improves test-time scaling\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 7\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Unstructured pruning can augment test-time scaling; structured pruning degrades it\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Motivates why structured pruning needs recovery; we address this gap with RLVR\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: should-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2604.25098\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: gprune_llm_2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"GPrune-LLM: Generalization-Aware Structured Pruning for Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Mar 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Cross-distribution generalization-aware pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 6\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Accounts for neuron cross-distribution behavior; reduces calibration bias\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Complementary importance metric; our CKA captures functional overlap vs their generalization gap\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: should-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2603.13418\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: boiling_frog_2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Gradually Compacting Large Language Models for Reasoning Like a Boiling Frog\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yiran Zhao, Shengyang Zhou, Zijian Wu, Tongyan Hu, Yuhui Xu, Rengan Dou, Kenji Kawaguchi, Shafiq Joty, Junnan Li, Michael Qizhe Shieh\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Feb 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Iterative prune-tune loop for reasoning model compression\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 7\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Gradual Prune-Tune Loop avoids abrupt performance collapse; iterative pruning+finetuning preserves reasoning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Similar prune-then-recover paradigm but uses SFT recovery; we use RLVR which is more effective and add CKA-guided pruning selection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: must-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2602.04919\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: think_prune_train_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Think, Prune, Train, Improve: Scaling Reasoning without Scaling Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Caia Costello, Simon Guo, Anna Goldie, Azalia Mirhoseini\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Apr 2025 (Stanford Scaling Intelligence Lab)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: direct-competitor\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Self-training on pruned reasoning traces to improve small models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 6\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Iterative fine-tuning on ground-truth-pruned reasoning traces; Gemma2-9B matches LLaMA-3.1-70B on GSM8K\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Complementary — prunes reasoning traces (CoT) not model weights; could combine with our weight pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: nice-to-have\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2504.18116\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # === Method Components ===\\\\n  - id: mpruner_2024\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"MPruner: Optimizing Neural Network Size with CKA-Based Mutual Information Pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Aug 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"CKA for layer importance estimation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 8\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"CKA similarity between layers identifies redundant layers for removal; 50% parameter reduction with minimal accuracy loss\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"We adapt CKA from layer-level to width-level functional overlap prediction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: must-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2408.13482\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: lachance_thesis_2024\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Using Centered Kernel Alignment for Understanding and Pruning Neural Networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Lachance\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"URI Master's Thesis\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"CKA-based pruning theoretical foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 6\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"CKA layer similarity correlates with pruning recoverability\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Validates CKA as signal for pruning decisions; we extend to predict RLVR recovery\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: should-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: fang_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"FANG: Improving Generalization in LLM Structured Pruning via Function-Aware Neuron Grouping\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Tao Yu, Yongqi An, Kuan Zhu, Guibo Zhu, Ming Tang, Jinqiao Wang\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Dec 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Function-aware neuron grouping for structured pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 7\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Groups FFN neurons by functional roles; shared neuron retention prevents cross-task accuracy loss; outperforms FLAP/OBC by 1.5-8.5% at 30-40% sparsity\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Closest conceptual parallel — both identify functionally critical neurons, but FANG uses activation-based grouping while we use CKA similarity; no recovery component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: must-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2512.23014\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: funcnet_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Pruning Large Language Models by Identifying and Preserving Functional Networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yiheng Liu, Junhao Ning, Sichen Xia, Xiaohui Gao, Ning Qiang, Bao Ge, Junwei Han, Xintao Hu\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Aug 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"ICA-based functional network identification for pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 7\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Applies ICA (from neuroimaging) to decompose LLM into functional networks; preserves key neurons within identified networks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Similar motivation — treat LLM as digital brain and preserve functional structure — but uses ICA vs our CKA; no RLVR recovery\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: must-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2508.05239\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: bonsai_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Bonsai: Gradient-Free Structured Pruning for LLMs\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICML 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Gradient-free structured pruning alternative\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 6\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Achieves competitive structured pruning without backprop\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Alternative pruning strategy; our CKA metric is also gradient-free\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: should-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: pat_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"PAT: Pruning-Aware Tuning for Large Language Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Yijiang Liu et al.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"AAAI 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Joint pruning and tuning framework via Hybrid Sparsification Modules\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 6\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Co-optimizing pruning mask and fine-tuning via HSMs; surpasses LoRA-64 by 1.26% at 25% pruning on Llama2-7B\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Related idea of pruning-tuning interaction; we separate pruning and RLVR recovery\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: should-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2408.14721\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: rac_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"RAC: Chain-of-Thought Reconstruction for Pruned Reasoning Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"CoT reconstruction post-pruning\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 7\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Reconstructing CoT improves unstructured/2:4 pruned reasoning models\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Complementary recovery strategy; could combine with our RLVR approach\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: should-cite\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: paser_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"PASER: Data Selection for Pruning Recovery\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"under review\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Recovery training data selection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 6\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Selective data for recovery training improves efficiency\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Orthogonal contribution; can apply PASER data selection to our RLVR recovery\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: nice-to-have\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: dppo_2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"DPPO: Unbiased Dynamic Pruning for Efficient Group-Based Policy Optimization\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Mar 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Rollout pruning to accelerate GRPO training\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 5\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Importance-sampling-based rollout pruning achieves 2.37x GRPO speedup with 3.36% accuracy gain on Qwen3-4B\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Could accelerate our GRPO-based RLVR recovery phase\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: nice-to-have\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2603.04135\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: arrol_2026\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"ARRoL: Prune as You Generate — Online Rollout Pruning for Faster and Better RLVR\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv Mar 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Online rollout pruning for RLVR efficiency\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 5\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Lightweight quality head predicts rollout success probability for early pruning during RLVR\\\\\\\"\\\\n    our_relation: \\\\\\\"Complementary technique for speeding up RLVR recovery training\\\\\\\"\\\\n    citation_priority: nice-to-have\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2603.24840\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - id: restorelcc_2025\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"RestoreLCC: Restoring Pruned Large Language Models via Lost Component Compensation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors: \\\\\\\"Zijian Feng, Hanzhang Zhou, Zixiao Zhu, Tianjiao Li, Jia Jim Deryl Chua, Lee Onn Mak, Gee Wah Ng, Kezhi Mao\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS 2025 (Spotlight, top 10%)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: method-component\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"Plug-and-play pruning recovery via activation compensation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: 6\\\\n    key_finding: \\\\\\\"Contrastively probes critical a